== Emulators & licensing

NES — src/nes/ is copied and modified from Esp32-S3-nes-emulator-by-DSN (https://github.com/derdacavga/Esp32-S3-nes-emulator-by-DSN) imported at commit 030c4b8.
Some modifications are made.

Game Boy — src/gb/ is copied and modified from Peanut-GB (https://github.com/deltabeard/Peanut-GB) .
Some modifications are made.

== License

The upstream NES emulator code is licensed under the GNU General Public
License v3 (see the LICENSE file, copied from the DSN repository; the
Nofrendo core originates as GPL‑licensed code by Matthew Conte). src/nes/ in
this repository is a derivative work and remains under the GPL.

Peanut-GB and minigb_apu (src/gb/) are under the MIT License (see
src/gb/peanut_gb.h and src/gb/LICENSE.minigb_apu); their notices are retained.
MIT imposes no copyleft, but this code is combined into the same binary as the
GPL NES core, so the paragraph below applies to the whole firmware regardless.

Because the yomogame firmware links this GPL code into a single program,
any distribution of a built yomogame binary (or of a device running it) is
subject to the GPL: recipients must be able to obtain the complete
corresponding source code under the same terms. For that reason this repository
as a whole is distributed under GPL‑3.0‑or‑later.

The first‑party parts of this project (lib/audio, lib/input,
lib/volume_overlay, src/tetris/, src/scene.h, src/frame_pusher.h,
src/yomogame.h, src/main.cpp, src/gb/gb_scene.h, src/gb/gb_core.c) are
written by the yomogame author. They are released here under the GPL as part of
the combined work.

